 "comment": "Hero landmarks: handmade models that replace (and hide) the procedural building at a spot. One entry per hero: where it is (lat/lng; fp = footprint [[lng,lat]...] when known; osm = the OSM way id 'w123' when known), the model (glb, relative to web/; null = the procedural building stays and only the label shows), how it sits (scale, rot = yaw in degrees or null to face the footprint's long side, offset = [east, up, north] metres), h = height in metres to fit to, clear = metres around the pin whose procedural buildings are hidden once the model is in, label + glow for the map. status: label (no model yet), live (model in), proposed (on the list, not approved). landmark: true for famous places: with no model yet the map still makes them stand out (their building grows to h with a glowing crown in the glow colour; shape \"tower\" puts up a placeholder tower of h metres, radius = its shaft in metres, and clears procedural buildings within clear). retired_glb = the old Tripo model kept for reference (not shown). Pipeline: scripts/hero_landmark.py; see docs/map_city.md.",
